Disclaimer: I'm a lot less experienced than other posters,
and I also don't play very carefully -- if I can ascend 25%
of the time with an Elbereth-heavy strategy, or 10% of the
time otherwise, I'll play the second way, because I usually
find Elbereth-camping pretty dull. So take what I say with
a grain of salt. OTOH, it seemed to me that the original
poster might feel the same way, and I'm not actually
suicidal.

So in re James's point about picking up scrolls,that was
a brain cramp on my part. If you don't want to take the
risk of crumbling a scare monster and owing the shopkeeper
100+zm, you should #chat in order to find out their price
(and then pick them up to #name them, if it's safe).

About ?oSM vs. Elbereth, isn't the main advantage of
the scroll the 0% failure rate?  If you need a monster to
stop bothering you right away, writing in the dust might
be risky, but the scroll is bound to work. (Note for the
newbie: ?oSM doesn't work against Elbereth-resistant
monsters. I kind of think it should, because it's a scarce
resource and Elbereth can be written any time, but I'm
not the DevTeam.)

Also, about hard gems and hard rings -- I believe those
take eight turns to put down an Elbereth, so don't use
them in emergencies! But if you can engrave in the floor
with a gem, it's bound to be worth at least 900 zm, 1500
if it's not yellowish-brown. If you formally identify it, you
can sell it to the Minetown general store (if there is one)
for protection money. I've used this after visiting Mines'
End, which in some versions guarantees a stack of gems
that's enough to clear out the shopkeeper. If you aren't
keeping your EXP down it won't get you past the first
donation, though -- shopkkepers have 1030-4000 zm
plus whatever you've given them, according to wikihack.

